  "steps": [
    "Whisk everything together until smooth. Cut a few shallow slashes into bone-in pieces so the marinade gets in.",
    "Add the chicken, turn to coat, cover (or seal in a zip-top bag) and refrigerate for at least 4 hours, ideally overnight, up to 24 hours.",
    "Scrape off the excess and cook hot: 450°F (230°C) oven, grill or broiler, until charred in spots.",
    "Never reuse marinade that has touched raw chicken. If you want extra for drizzling, set some aside before adding the chicken."
